// **the one thing a `while` cannot express.** a `for`'s continue target is its step block, not its
// condition - so the increment runs on the way round and the loop terminates. written as a `while` with
// the increment at the top of the body, `continue` would skip it and this would never end
for (int32 $i = 0; $i < 6; $i++) {
    if ($i == 3) {
        continue;
    }
    echo $i;
}
